        </time>
        <geography>
            <locationOfOperationSupplyOrProduction location="RER" latitudeAndLongitude="55.895602991909776;28.119894957029818">
                <descriptionOfRestrictions xml:lang="en">Mainly based on EU studies. ETBE is largely produced in France, Spain and possibly soon in Germany.</descriptionOfRestrictions>
            </locationOfOperationSupplyOrProduction>
        </geography>
        <technology>
            <technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses xml:lang="en">Production of ETBE according to the IFP technology\n\n# Included processes\nThis process includes the production of ethyl tert-butyl ether (ETBE), at the oil refinery. ETBE is the result of the reaction between 45.1% wt. anhydrous ethanol from biomass and 54.9% wt. isobutene (side-product of oil refineries).</technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>
        </technology>
    </processInformation>
